1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,350
Here is a country that is home to the oldest
European city in the Americas.

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:09,628
This is the Dominican Republic, known as
Quisqueya, mother of all lands.

3
00:00:09,968 --> 00:00:11,845
Its capital is Santo Domingo.

4
00:00:12,265 --> 00:00:16,450
About ten point eight million people livee
here, on about forty-eight thousand

5
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:17,420
square kilometers.

6
00:00:18,002 --> 00:00:20,482
They speak a Caribbean Spanish.

7
00:00:20,502 --> 00:00:21,611
Hello is hola.

8
00:00:21,922 --> 00:00:23,814
And they pay with the Dominican peso.

9
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:24,647
Some fun facts.

10
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,280
And stay until the end, for a
mystery nobody ever solved.

11
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:35,387
The highest peak in the Caribbean, and its
lowest point, are both in this one

12
00:00:35,407 --> 00:00:35,855
country.

13
00:00:35,875 --> 00:00:40,537
Pico Duarte rises over three thousand meters,
and Lake Enriquillo sits below sea

14
00:00:40,557 --> 00:00:40,888
level.

15
00:00:41,484 --> 00:00:45,759
Larimar, a pale blue stone, is found only
in the Dominican Republic.

16
00:00:46,148 --> 00:00:51,328
Dominican amber often holds insects from
prehistoric times, trapped inside like

17
00:00:51,348 --> 00:00:52,579
tiny time capsules.

18
00:00:53,367 --> 00:00:55,047
Now, a few surprising places.

19
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,637
Near Puerto Plata, the Damajagua
waterfalls form a staircase of natural

20
00:01:01,657 --> 00:01:04,847
limestone pools that you can
climb and slide down.

21
00:01:05,235 --> 00:01:09,965
In Santo Domingo, Los Tres Ojos are lakes
hidden inside a limestone cave.

22
00:01:10,843 --> 00:01:15,688
In the far southwest, Bahía de las Aguilas is
a remote beach inside a national

23
00:01:15,708 --> 00:01:16,000
park.

24
00:01:16,739 --> 00:01:21,344
And Los Haitises National Park hides
rainforest, mangroves and caves along the

25
00:01:21,364 --> 00:01:22,293
northeast coast.

26
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,280
So, what does ten dollars get you here?

27
00:01:26,933 --> 00:01:29,389
A cappuccino costs about two
and a half dollars.

28
00:01:29,762 --> 00:01:32,130
A local beer costs about two and
a half dollars too.

29
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,394
And a Coke costs about one dollar.

30
00:01:34,745 --> 00:01:38,336
So with ten dollars, you get a
coffee, a beer and a soda.

31
00:01:38,356 --> 00:01:42,011
But a short taxi ride downtown costs
about twenty dollars.

32
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,180
Now, the don't list.

33
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:47,076
Don't take a street taxi.

34
00:01:47,096 --> 00:01:50,470
Book one through your hotel, and
agree on the price first.

35
00:01:50,892 --> 00:01:52,848
Don't leave your drink unattended.

36
00:01:53,565 --> 00:01:55,747
Don't walk alone on empty
beaches at night.

37
00:01:56,219 --> 00:01:58,215
Don't dive into unfamiliar water.

38
00:01:58,235 --> 00:02:01,759
Drownings happen every year, and
there are few lifeguards.

39
00:02:02,245 --> 00:02:05,683
And don't carry anything for someone
else, not even cannabis.

40
00:02:05,703 --> 00:02:09,707
The country has zero tolerance for drugs,
and you can be held for up to

41
00:02:09,727 --> 00:02:11,578
forty-eight hours without charge.

42
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:13,297
Let's talk about culture.

43
00:02:14,867 --> 00:02:19,149
The national lunch is La Bandera:
rice, red beans, and meat.

44
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:24,726
For breakfast, many Dominicans eat mangú:
mashed green plantains with fried

45
00:02:24,746 --> 00:02:27,183
onions, eggs, salami and fried cheese.

46
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:32,990
And the music is merengue, played with an
accordion, a tambora drum and a güira

47
00:02:33,010 --> 00:02:33,481
scraper.

48
00:02:33,501 --> 00:02:36,858
UNESCO added it to its heritage
list in twenty sixteen.

49
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:38,847
Time for a little history.

50
00:02:40,367 --> 00:02:44,727
In fourteen ninety-six, Bartholomew Columbus
founded Santo Domingo, the oldest

51
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:47,760
European city in the Americas that
is still inhabited.

52
00:02:48,031 --> 00:02:52,339
In eighteen forty-four, after twenty-two years
under Haitian rule, the country

53
00:02:52,359 --> 00:02:55,669
declared its independence on the
twenty-seventh of February.

54
00:02:56,121 --> 00:03:00,191
From nineteen thirty to nineteen sixty-one,
Rafael Trujillo ruled the country

55
00:03:00,211 --> 00:03:02,740
for thirty-one years, until he
was assassinated.

56
00:03:03,533 --> 00:03:07,413
And now, the chapter you were all waiting
for: legends and mysteries.

57
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,773
In Dominican folklore, there is a
creature called the Ciguapa.

58
00:03:12,793 --> 00:03:17,117
She is a woman with long dark hair and
feet that point backward, so her

59
00:03:17,137 --> 00:03:18,952
footprints lead the wrong way.

60
00:03:18,972 --> 00:03:23,724
She is said to appear at night in the
mountains, caves and rivers, and to lure

61
00:03:23,744 --> 00:03:24,275
men away.

62
00:03:24,295 --> 00:03:27,395
Where the story really comes
from is still debated.

63
00:03:27,863 --> 00:03:32,596
On the north coast near Puerto Plata, a beach
is named after the pirate Cofresí.

64
00:03:32,616 --> 00:03:37,230
According to legend, he used this coast as a
hideout and buried treasure taken

65
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,359
from Spanish ships.

66
00:03:38,379 --> 00:03:42,934
People still tell the story, and treasure
hunters still wonder where it might

67
00:03:42,954 --> 00:03:43,112
be.

68
00:03:43,411 --> 00:03:44,790
Then there is a mystery.

69
00:03:44,810 --> 00:03:49,218
When Columbus arrived in fourteen ninety-two,
the Taíno people lived on this

70
00:03:49,238 --> 00:03:49,626
island.

71
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:53,647
Disease and forced labor devastated their
communities within decades.

72
00:03:53,667 --> 00:03:56,910
And researchers still debate what
really became of them.

73
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:01,873
That was the Dominican Republic.

74
00:04:01,893 --> 00:04:03,888
Which country should we visit next?

75
00:04:03,908 --> 00:04:05,270
Tell me in the comments.

